From 6792f50e1694ab6bf8595543a636e2cfdfe92569 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reixo <125610085+Reixo0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:52:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 323/323] spi: qcom-geni: do not terminate GPI DMA from the panic
 notifier

The panic notifier calls dmaengine_terminate_async() on the GPI channels.
gpi_terminate_all() sends GPI commands and waits for their completion,
which sleeps. On a watchdog bark the panic runs from the idle thread: the
wait printed "bad: scheduling from the idle thread" in a loop, overwrote
the whole ramoops console and the panic never reached its reboot, so the
phone hung instead of restarting.

Leave GPI transfers alone in the notifier; the FIFO/SE DMA paths, which
only poll registers, are kept.

Fixes: b7b192e58f35 ("spi: qcom-geni: Add panic notifier to cancel and reset DMA during panic")
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c b/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
index 91e75e213f92..4dfd52babb6e 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
@@ -1093,11 +1093,15 @@ static int spi_geni_panic_notifier(struct notifier_block *nb,
 	if (!pm_runtime_active(mas->dev))
 		return NOTIFY_OK;
 
-	if (mas->cur_xfer_mode == GENI_GPI_DMA) {
-		dmaengine_terminate_async(mas->tx);
-		dmaengine_terminate_async(mas->rx);
+	/*
+	 * Leave GPI DMA alone: gpi_terminate_all() sends GPI commands and
+	 * waits for their completion, which sleeps. A panic notifier must
+	 * not sleep; from the idle thread (a watchdog bark) it printed
+	 * "scheduling from the idle thread" over and over, overwrote the
+	 * crash log and never let the panic reach its reboot.
+	 */
+	if (mas->cur_xfer_mode == GENI_GPI_DMA)
 		return NOTIFY_OK;
-	}
 
 	if (!(readl_relaxed(se->base + SE_GENI_STATUS) & M_GENI_CMD_ACTIVE))
 		return NOTIFY_OK;
